% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-28 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: systemic_amyloidosis (the AREA — the differential of systemic
% amyloid fibril TYPE / etiology in a multisystem infiltrative illness — NOT a
% specific named subtype).
%
% The diagnostic puzzle the IR poses (q1-q4): a 59-year-old man with ~10 weeks of
% crampy lower abdominal pain, bloating, borborygmi, loose pale (steatorrhoeic)
% stools 4x/day and ~18 kg weight loss (a MALABSORPTION picture); new
% length-dependent NUMBNESS of hands and feet with electrodiagnostically confirmed
% active peripheral NEUROPATHY; spontaneous BRUISE-LIKE PATCHES + petechiae over
% forearms/shins with no trauma (amyloid/vascular-fragility purpura); MACROGLOSSIA
% on exam; diffuse small-bowel wall thickening with a firm, GRANULAR, edematous
% cecum-to-ileum at laparotomy (mimicking peritonitis/IBD but NO perforation);
% profound HYPOALBUMINEMIA (22) and anemia (Hb 86); sub-nephrotic PROTEINURIA
% (910 mg/24h) with renal impairment (creatinine 205); a strongly INFLAMMATORY
% profile (CRP 188, IL-6 47, ESR 52); cardiac signal change on MRI with a small
% troponin/NT-proBNP rise; and primary hypothyroidism. Pivotally, the monoclonal /
% clonal workup is THOROUGHLY NEGATIVE: serum AND urine immunofixation negative,
% Bence-Jones absent, serum free light chains normal, immunoglobulins/CTD panel
% unremarkable, serum VEGF normal, and a NON-clonal marrow with only mild (7%)
% plasmacytosis.
%
% Unifying lesion: SYSTEMIC AMYLOIDOSIS. The firm/granular infiltrated bowel,
% macroglossia, vascular-fragility purpura, proteinuric nephropathy, peripheral
% neuropathy and patchy myocardial signal change are correlated manifestations of
% ONE infiltrative deposition process. The decision the case forces is the FIBRIL
% TYPE, because management diverges radically by type and because the negative
% clonal workup must be reconciled (q3).
%
% Candidates: aa_amyloidosis (reactive / inflammatory, SAA-driven),
% al_amyloidosis (immunoglobulin light chain — the TEMPTING answer because of the
% macroglossia + purpura gestalt), attr_amyloidosis (transthyretin — hereditary or
% wild-type, clonal-workup-negative), and poems_syndrome (a non-amyloid
% neuropathy/organ/skin mimic kept on the differential to be excluded).
%
% Magnitudes encoded QUALITATIVELY per adj-lang grammar (lowercase identifiers,
% no uppercase, no leading digit): crp(markedly_elevated), il6(elevated),
% proteinuria(sub_nephrotic), albumin(markedly_low), etc.
%
% Anti-overfit note: each clause is added because a cited source supports the
% DIRECTION of its likelihood ratio for that type, NOT to steer this case onto a
% chosen answer. The discriminators that argue AGAINST the tempting wrong answer
% (AL) — namely the COMPLETELY negative monoclonal/clonal workup, which makes AL
% a ~0.2% event in the Mayo series — fire with LR<1 because the sources support
% it, not because we want AA to win.
%
% CORRELATED EVIDENCE (anti-saturation): three distinct latent mechanisms.
%  (1) The amyloid infiltrative tissue syndrome (granular bowel, macroglossia,
%      purpura, proteinuria, neuropathy, cardiac signal) is ONE deposition process
%      shared by ALL amyloid types — grouped under a single mechanism that fires
%      ONCE per amyloid conclusion rather than summing one edge per organ.
%  (2) The acute-phase INFLAMMATORY signature (CRP markedly high, IL-6 high, ESR
%      high) is ONE SAA-driving mechanism specific to AA — grouped once for AA.
%  (3) The AL bleeding/soft-tissue gestalt (macroglossia + spontaneous purpura,
%      the classic factor-X / vascular-fragility AL picture) is grouped once for
%      AL as a (modest) AL-supportive mechanism, so the tongue+bruising is not
%      counted twice across both the shared-amyloid and AL-specific lines.
% What remain as independent `contributes` are the TYPE discriminators that
% actually separate the candidates (the clonal workup, the inflammatory driver as
% an AA-specific edge, VEGF, demographics, and the pending typing/genetic tests).
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates among new systemic amyloidosis diagnoses) =====

% rationale: AL (immunoglobulin light-chain) amyloidosis is the single commonest
% type of systemic amyloidosis in the developed world and the one most associated
% with macroglossia + amyloid purpura, so it carries the largest prior BEFORE the
% clonal workup is taken into account.
prior 0.42 for amyloid_type(al_amyloidosis)
  source "Wiley AJH 2024 update on AL amyloidosis diagnosis (AL is the commonest systemic amyloidosis)" trust authoritative

% rationale: AA (reactive / inflammatory) amyloidosis is the next commonest
% systemic type, driven by sustained serum amyloid A under chronic inflammation;
% renal involvement is near-universal.
prior 0.28 for amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis)
  source "Medscape 335559 AA (Inflammatory) Amyloidosis; PMC11219434 AA: A Contemporary View (renal involvement ~97%)" trust authoritative

% rationale: ATTR (transthyretin — hereditary variant or wild-type) is a major
% non-clonal systemic amyloidosis with a neuropathy + cardiac + GI phenotype;
% lower prior than AL/AA overall.
prior 0.22 for amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
  source "Frontiers Neurol 2023;14:1242815 hereditary ATTR review (neuropathy, nephropathy, cardiomyopathy, GI)" trust authoritative

% rationale: POEMS is a non-amyloid plasma-cell mimic (polyneuropathy,
% organomegaly, endocrinopathy, skin changes) kept on the differential because the
% neuropathy + skin + endocrine + multisystem picture superficially fits; modest
% prior, must be EARNED away on VEGF + paraprotein.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(poems_syndrome)
  source "Springer J Neurol 2018 POEMS clinical update; Orphanet POEMS diagnostic criteria" trust authoritative

% ===== SHARED AMYLOID INFILTRATIVE SYNDROME (count once per amyloid type) =====
% rationale: a firm/granular infiltrated small bowel, macroglossia, spontaneous
% vascular-fragility purpura, proteinuric nephropathy, peripheral neuropathy and
% patchy non-thickening myocardial signal change are correlated effects of ONE
% mechanism — extracellular amyloid fibril deposition in multiple organs. Fire
% ONCE per amyloid conclusion rather than summing six organ edges (anti-double-
% count). The magnitude is the same across amyloid types because this gestalt
% confirms AMYLOID, not its TYPE; typing is done by the discriminators below.
% mechanism amyloid_infiltration for amyloid_type(al_amyloidosis) lr 8.0 : bowel_infiltration(firm_granular), macroglossia(present), purpura(spontaneous_nontraumatic), proteinuria(sub_nephrotic), peripheral_neuropathy(active), cardiac_signal_change(present)
% mechanism amyloid_infiltration for amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis) lr 8.0 : bowel_infiltration(firm_granular), macroglossia(present), purpura(spontaneous_nontraumatic), proteinuria(sub_nephrotic), peripheral_neuropathy(active), cardiac_signal_change(present)
% mechanism amyloid_infiltration for amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis) lr 8.0 : bowel_infiltration(firm_granular), macroglossia(present), purpura(spontaneous_nontraumatic), proteinuria(sub_nephrotic), peripheral_neuropathy(active), cardiac_signal_change(present)

% ===== AA-SPECIFIC ACUTE-PHASE / SAA-DRIVING MECHANISM (count once for AA) =====
% rationale: a markedly elevated CRP, high IL-6 and high ESR are correlated
% acute-phase manifestations of ONE upstream process — sustained inflammatory
% (IL-6 -> hepatic SAA) drive, which is the PREREQUISITE for AA fibrillogenesis.
% Group them so the inflammatory burst fires the AA-supporting LR ONCE rather than
% three times. This same signature is the strongest argument that the amyloid here
% is REACTIVE (AA) rather than light-chain.
% mechanism saa_acute_phase_drive for amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis) lr 5.5 : crp(markedly_elevated), il6(elevated), esr(elevated)

% rationale (AA discriminator, NEGATIVE for AL): AL amyloidosis is a plasma-cell /
% light-chain disease, NOT an inflammatory one; a markedly elevated acute-phase
% response is not its mechanism and points away from AL toward a reactive process.
contributes 0.6 from crp(markedly_elevated) to amyloid_type(al_amyloidosis)
  source "CrackMedicine AL vs AA (AL is light-chain driven, not acute-phase/inflammatory)" trust empirical

% ===== AL-SPECIFIC BLEEDING / SOFT-TISSUE GESTALT (count once for AL) =====
% rationale: macroglossia together with spontaneous bruising/purpura is the
% classic AL soft-tissue + vascular-fragility (factor-X adsorption / amyloid
% angiopathy) picture; tongue amyloid is "almost always" AL. Grouped as ONE
% modest AL-supporting mechanism so the tongue+bruising findings are not also
% re-summed on top of the shared-amyloid line (which already credits them to all
% types). LR kept modest because macroglossia is suggestive of AL but not
% type-defining on its own, and ATTR can also enlarge the tongue.
% mechanism al_soft_tissue_bleeding for amyloid_type(al_amyloidosis) lr 2.2 : macroglossia(present), purpura(spontaneous_nontraumatic)
%   source "ASH Blood 116:5007 Macroglossia not always AL; Blood 97:1885 acquired factor X deficiency in AL"

% ===== MONOCLONAL / CLONAL WORKUP — THE KEY TYPE DISCRIMINATOR =====

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE against the tempting AL answer) — a
% COMPLETELY negative monoclonal screen (serum AND urine immunofixation negative,
% Bence-Jones absent, serum free light chains normal) makes AL extremely unlikely:
% in the Mayo series only ~0.2% of AL patients had ALL monoclonal-protein studies
% normal. This is the single strongest argument the amyloid here is NON-AL.
contributes 0.05 from clonal_workup(fully_negative) to amyloid_type(al_amyloidosis)
  source "Mayo / PMC10164359 & Haematologica SFLC eval (only ~0.2% of AL have all monoclonal studies normal)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a fully negative monoclonal/clonal screen is exactly what is EXPECTED
% in reactive AA amyloidosis (polyclonal, inflammation-driven, no paraprotein),
% so it is consistent-to-supportive rather than against.
contributes 1.4 from clonal_workup(fully_negative) to amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis)
  source "Medscape 335559 AA workup; Wikipedia AA amyloidosis (polyclonal, no monoclonal protein)" trust authoritative

% rationale: ATTR is a transthyretin (non-immunoglobulin) amyloid; a negative
% monoclonal/clonal workup is fully consistent with ATTR and is in fact required
% before attributing neuropathy to a paraprotein — supportive of a non-clonal type.
contributes 1.3 from clonal_workup(fully_negative) to amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
  source "Frontiers Neurol 2023;14:1242815; Springer J Neurol 2019 ATTR-PN consensus (exclude paraprotein; TTR sequencing)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE against POEMS) — POEMS REQUIRES a
% monoclonal plasma-cell disorder (mandatory criterion, almost always lambda); a
% thoroughly negative paraprotein workup with a non-clonal marrow argues strongly
% against POEMS.
contributes 0.1 from clonal_workup(fully_negative) to diagnosis(poems_syndrome)
  source "Springer J Neurol 2018 POEMS update; Orphanet POEMS criteria (monoclonal plasma-cell disorder mandatory)" trust authoritative

% ===== VEGF — POEMS DISCRIMINATOR =====

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires NEGATIVE against POEMS) — a NORMAL serum
% VEGF argues against POEMS, in which VEGF (a major criterion) is characteristically
% elevated; combined with the absent paraprotein this effectively excludes POEMS.
contributes 0.2 from vegf(normal) to diagnosis(poems_syndrome)
  source "Springer J Neurol 2018 POEMS update; HemaSphere 2022 POEMS dx (elevated VEGF is a major criterion)" trust authoritative

% ===== INDEPENDENT AA-vs-AL / TYPE EDGES =====

% rationale: heavy / progressive proteinuric renal involvement is near-universal in
% AA (~97%) and is its dominant clinical mode; supports AA modestly. (Kept small
% and SEPARATE from the shared amyloid-infiltration line, which credited the renal
% deposition to all types equally; this edge captures the AA-specific renal
% PREDOMINANCE, not the mere presence of proteinuria.)
contributes 1.6 from renal_predominant(present) to amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis)
  source "PMC11219434 AA: A Contemporary View; Medscape 335559 (renal involvement ~97% in AA)" trust authoritative

% rationale: macroglossia is reported "almost always" with AL (and ATTR) and is
% atypical for AA; so the presence of macroglossia is a mild edge AGAINST a purely
% reactive AA type. Kept modest (LR<1 but near 1) because idiopathic/reactive AA
% can rarely involve the tongue and the inflammatory data still dominate.
contributes 0.8 from macroglossia(present) to amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis)
  source "ASH Blood 116:5007 Macroglossia - Not Always AL; MyAmyloidosisTeam (tongue amyloid usually AL/ATTR)" trust empirical

% rationale: an older male with a neuropathy + cardiac phenotype is the typical
% ATTR demographic; mildly supportive of ATTR.
contributes 1.3 from demographic(older_male) to amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
  source "Frontiers Neurol 2023;14:1242815 hereditary ATTR review (adult-onset, male-predominant in many series)" trust empirical

% rationale: a markedly inflammatory acute-phase state is NOT a feature of ATTR
% (a non-inflammatory deposition disease); the strong CRP/IL-6/ESR profile argues
% mildly against ATTR being the unifying type. LR<1.
contributes 0.7 from crp(markedly_elevated) to amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
  source "Frontiers Neurol 2023;14:1242815 (ATTR is non-inflammatory; no acute-phase signature)" trust inferred

% ===== SYNERGY =====

% rationale: KEY SYNERGY — a markedly elevated acute-phase response TOGETHER with a
% fully negative monoclonal workup is the defining combination of REACTIVE (AA)
% amyloidosis: sustained inflammation drives SAA fibrillogenesis with NO paraprotein.
% The two independent lines (inflammation present + clonality absent) reinforce.
interacts 2.0 when crp(markedly_elevated) and clonal_workup(fully_negative) for amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis)
  source "CrackMedicine AL vs AA; PMC11219434 AA (chronic inflammation + no monoclonal protein -> AA)" trust authoritative

% ===== DECISION-RELEVANT UNCERTAINTIES =====
% The unresolved tests that move the TYPE posterior are (a) amyloid TYPING on tissue
% biopsy (mass-spectrometry / immunohistochemistry of the Congo-red-positive
% deposit) and (b) TTR gene sequencing. Each candidate result has a contributes
% edge below, so resolving the uncertainty shifts the posterior.

% rationale: amyloid typing that identifies SERUM AMYLOID A protein in the deposit
% is confirmatory for AA — near-decisive when present.
contributes 7.0 from amyloid_typing(serum_amyloid_a) to amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis)
  source "Mayo Clin Proc 2020 amyloid typing by mass spectrometry (subtype identified by deposit protein)" trust authoritative

% rationale: amyloid typing identifying immunoglobulin LIGHT CHAIN in the deposit
% would confirm AL despite a negative serum screen (rare AL with normal monoclonal
% studies typed on tissue); strong edge for AL.
contributes 7.0 from amyloid_typing(immunoglobulin_light_chain) to amyloid_type(al_amyloidosis)
  source "ASH Blood 120:3206 How I treat amyloidosis (tissue typing by mass spec is decisive for subtype)" trust authoritative

% rationale: amyloid typing identifying TRANSTHYRETIN protein in the deposit, or a
% pathogenic TTR variant on sequencing, confirms ATTR; strong edge for ATTR.
contributes 7.0 from amyloid_typing(transthyretin) to amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
  source "ARUP TTR sequencing; Mayo Clin Proc 2020 amyloid typing (TTR fibril identifies ATTR)" trust authoritative

contributes 5.0 from ttr_gene(pathogenic_variant) to amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
  source "ARUP Familial Transthyretin Amyloidosis TTR Sequencing (pathogenic variant confirms hereditary ATTR)" trust authoritative

uncertain { amyloid_typing(serum_amyloid_a), amyloid_typing(immunoglobulin_light_chain), amyloid_typing(transthyretin) } for amyloid_type(aa_amyloidosis)
uncertain { amyloid_typing(immunoglobulin_light_chain), amyloid_typing(serum_amyloid_a), amyloid_typing(transthyretin) } for amyloid_type(al_amyloidosis)
uncertain { amyloid_typing(transthyretin), amyloid_typing(serum_amyloid_a), amyloid_typing(immunoglobulin_light_chain) } for amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
uncertain { ttr_gene(pathogenic_variant), ttr_gene(no_variant) } for amyloid_type(attr_amyloidosis)
